{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And they shall put it on the two doorposts and on the lintel.</b> And Moshe reversed the order and said, ״וְהִגַּעְתֶּם אֶל הַמַּשְׁקוֹף וְאֶל שְׁתֵּי הַמְּזוּזוֹת״ ( Exodus 12:22). And according to the way of the midrash (Eikhah Rabbah 5:21), we may say that they said that the Holy One, blessed be He, said to Israel (Malachi 3:7), ״שׁוּבוּ אֵלַי תְּחִלָּה — return to Me first,״ and afterward, ״וְאָשׁוּבָה אֲלֵיכֶם — and I will return to you.״ And the congregation of Israel replies: ״I have no strength to return first; rather, You be the one to begin,״ as it says (Lamentations 5:21), ״הֲשִׁיבֵנוּ ה׳ אֵלֶיךָ — restore us, HaShem, to You,״ and afterward, ״וְנָשׁוּבָה — and we will return.״ And in this manner one may explain the mashqof as referring to the Name, blessed be He exalted, who is above all, as it states (Psalms 102:20), ״כִּי הִשְׁקִיף מִמְּרוֹם קָדְשׁוֹ — for He looked down from the height of His sanctuary.״ And the two doorposts that support the lintel — these are the merit of the fathers and the mothers, as it is written (Deuteronomy 33:27), ״מְעֹנָה אֱלֹהֵי קֶדֶם וּמִתַּחַת זְרֹעֹת עוֹלָם — the dwelling-place of the God of old, and underneath, the arms of eternity,״ for the fathers are beneath the divine chariot and they are the arms of eternity. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, said — as one who gives honor to those who fear Him — ״וְנָתְנוּ עַל שְׁתֵּי הַמְּזוּזוֹת״ first, and afterward ״וְעַל הַמַּשְׁקוֹף,״ to say that the righteous, the children of the fathers and mothers, shall be the ones who begin. But Moshe said ״וְהִגַּעְתֶּם אֶל הַמַּשְׁקוֹף״ first, for we have no strength to begin." "And there are those who say that it follows the path that Rashi explained in Shir HaShirim (Song of Songs 7:2), that Israel praises the Holy One, blessed be He, from above to below, and the Holy One, blessed be He, counts their praise from below to above. Therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, placed the doorposts before the lintel, to say that the influx ascends from below, for the righteous add strength to the power on high. However, for the sake of honor, Moshe placed the lintel before the doorposts, to say that the influx descends from above to below, for this is the way of honor toward the Name, blessed be He. And if you wish to say that the two doorposts correspond to Moshe and Aharon, that too will come out correctly, for the Holy One, blessed be He, apportioned them honor, and they apportioned honor to the Name, blessed be He."], :book :exodus, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 12, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:19:35.910630873Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}